{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01HBcnb6WeUE3TQdUXMuS42y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"- **It's a personal productivity / task-management system** for J.C. Liechty â€” markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files, plus cancelled/saved/weekly-review archives) are the source of truth; no database, no syncing, all living in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`).\n\n- **It ships a self-contained Python web app, `anchor_gui.py`** â€” a stdlib-only local HTTP server (bound to `localhost:8777`, run persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`) that generates an interactive browser dashboard and reads/writes the markdown directly. Users check off tasks, add tasks, and capture ideas in the browser; every change is saved back to markdown and logged.\n\n- **It ships a CLI mirror, `anchor.py`** â€” the same read/write/HTML-generation logic as command-line commands (`done`, `add`, `capture`, `cancel`, `save`, `restore`, `dashboard`), plus a static `dashboard.html` generator, used as the fallback when the GUI can't launch.\n\n- **Tasks move through a defined lifecycle** â€” Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored â€” each state backed by its own markdown file, with optional Notes fields for context.\n\n- **It has a self-test/health system** â€” `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM (Task Scheduler), parsing every file, booting a throwaway test server, exercising every endpoint and the full task lifecycle, and writing dated reports to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **The bulk of recent development is an \"R&D Control Surface\"** built up across versions v2 â†’ v3 â†’ v4 (\"Project Cockpit\", merged to master 2026-06-13). This turns each project's window into a **cockpit for \"trio\"-driven R&D work** (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio): per-lane status tiles with one honest status light, inline expanding panels, real interactive **ConPTY terminals** isolated in per-session git worktrees, cached/validated AI-generated session+project summaries, an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), cost/tokens/time rollups, a grass-catcher idea board, and type-aware deliverable launching.\n\n- **It's deliberately dependency-light** â€” Python 3.8+ stdlib only, with **one declared exception**: the optional `pywinpty` native dep for the v3/v4 terminal subsystem (lazy-imported in `pty_manager.py` only, degrades gracefully if absent). A `distro.py` import scanner enforces this rule.\n\n- **It's branded as a Ghost World Labs tool** (\"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\"), using a vendored brand mark for the dashboard masthead and favicon.\n\nThese claims are grounded in the project's `CLAUDE.md` and the locked North Star / design-decision anchors from the v3/v4 planning docs."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4420,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45832,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a185ace6-6d8d-4100-8e7b-41ae8a455106","uuid":"a18a3e3b-d7e0-4424-b106-23f64f6bbdde","request_id":"req_011Cc2KLnWHLZ4ASTNaYhW8G"}
